## 0. CONFIDENCE SYSTEM — GOVERNS ALL DECISIONS

Every finding carries a CONFIDENCE score from 0.0 to 1.0.

Scoring rules:
1.00 → AST tool returned exact result (ast-grep, ts-morph, javap)
0.85 → Multiple grep patterns corroborate each other
0.70 → Single grep pattern, no corroboration
0.50 → Structural inference from file/folder naming
0.30 → Pattern match from training knowledge
0.00 → No evidence

CONFIDENCE thresholds:

> = 0.85 → ANALYZER proceeds autonomously
> = 0.70 → ANALYZER proceeds, flags for CHALLENGER scrutiny
> <  0.70 → HARD STOP → raise CONFIDENCE_BLOCKER → wait for human

CONFIDENCE_BLOCKER format:
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ CONFIDENCE_BLOCKER                                       │
│ Finding: {what the agent was trying to determine}        │
│ Best confidence achieved: {score}                        │
│ Evidence available: {what was found}                     │
│ Evidence missing: {what would raise confidence}          │
│ Options:                                                 │
│   A) Provide {specific file or data} to continue        │
│   B) Accept {score} confidence and proceed at your risk │
│   C) Skip this finding and document as UNRESOLVED       │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

