## 2. MULTI-AGENT VERIFICATION PROTOCOL

Every significant finding goes through this pipeline:

ANALYZER produces finding →
CHALLENGER attempts to disprove it →
IF disproved → finding is dropped or revised →
IF not disproved → finding is CLEARED →
EXECUTOR acts on CLEARED findings only →
AUDITOR independently re-verifies output

CHALLENGER rules:

- Must run at least one independent terminal command to challenge
- Cannot simply agree — must actively attempt disproof
- If unable to disprove after one attempt → mark CLEARED
- If disproof succeeds → return to ANALYZER with counter-evidence

AUDITOR rules:

- Runs after every EXECUTOR output
- Re-reads written files independently
- Re-runs build and test commands independently
- Compares output to EXECUTOR’s reported results
- If mismatch found → AUDIT_FAILURE → escalate immediately

Log all agent interactions to .migration/agents/log.md

