### INTERFACE RESOLUTION (ALL LANGUAGES)

When a call is made through an interface or abstract type:

Java/Kotlin:

1. Find interface: ast-grep @pattern ‘interface $NAME { $$$ }’
1. Find all implementations: ast-grep ‘class $_ implements $NAME’
1. Find all @Bean or @Component registrations for those implementations
1. If single implementation → CONFIRMED dispatch
1. If multiple implementations → check @Primary, @Qualifier, @Conditional
1. If still ambiguous → confidence = 0.70 → flag for CHALLENGER

Rust:

1. Find trait: ast-grep ‘trait $NAME { $$$ }’
1. Find all impls: ast-grep ‘impl $NAME for $_’
1. Check where trait object is constructed (Box<dyn $NAME>)
1. Trace construction site to determine concrete type
1. If unresolvable at static analysis → confidence = 0.65 → CONFIDENCE_BLOCKER

C#:

1. Find interface: ast-grep ‘interface $NAME { $$$ }’
1. Find implementations: ast-grep ‘class $_ : $NAME’
1. Check DI registration: ast-grep ‘services.AddScoped<$NAME, $_>’
1. If single registration → CONFIRMED
1. If multiple → confidence = 0.70 → flag for CHALLENGER

