STEP 3.4 — Detect Cross-Service Transactions (HARD BLOCKER SOURCE)

Find all @Transactional boundaries:
Java/Kotlin:
Terminal: ast-grep –lang java   
–pattern ‘@Transactional($$$) public $RET $METHOD($$$) { $$$ }’   
–json . 2>/dev/null

C#:
Terminal: ast-grep –lang csharp   
–pattern ‘using var transaction = $CONTEXT.Database.BeginTransaction();’   
–json . 2>/dev/null

Rust:
Terminal: ast-grep –lang rust   
–pattern ‘let mut tx = $POOL.begin().await’   
–json . 2>/dev/null

For each transaction boundary found:
Trace which tables are written inside the transaction boundary.
Cross-reference with module-table-map.json.
IF transaction writes to tables that belong to different proposed services:
→ CROSS_SERVICE_TRANSACTION detected
→ This is a HARD_BLOCKER for splitting those services
→ Must be resolved before extraction proceeds

Write .migration/db/cross-service-transactions.json:
{
“transactions”: [
{
“location”: “{file}:{line}”,
“method”: “{class}.{method}”,
“tables_written”: [”{table1}”, “{table2}”],
