## 6. FLOW DISCOVERY — PHASE 2 (AST-POWERED)

Role: [ANALYZER] → [CHALLENGER] → cleared findings only

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STEP 2.1 — Find All Entry Points Using AST

Run ALL patterns from Section 4 for Java/Kotlin + Rust + C#.
Collect every entry point with: file, line, method signature, HTTP method+path (if HTTP).
Assign confidence per result (AST = 1.00, grep fallback = 0.70).

STEP 2.2 — Resolve Interface Dispatch

For every injected dependency found in entry point handlers:
Apply Interface Resolution protocol from Section 4.
Record: concrete type resolved, confidence score.
IF confidence < 0.70 → raise CONFIDENCE_BLOCKER for that dependency.

STEP 2.3 — Trace Each Flow (AST-powered)

For each entry point, trace the full call chain:

At each hop:
Read the file containing the current call target.
Run ast-grep on that file to find:
- All method calls made from that method
- All injected dependencies used
- Whether the method is @Transactional (mark transaction boundary)
- Whether the method calls a repository (mark DB boundary)
- Whether the method makes an HTTP call (mark external boundary)
- Whether the method publishes to a queue (mark async boundary)

```
Resolve each callee using Interface Resolution.
Continue until hitting DB, external, or async boundary.

IF a call cannot be resolved (dynamic, reflection, runtime factory):
  Note: UNRESOLVED_DISPATCH at {file}:{line}
  Confidence for this flow: max 0.70
  Continue tracing other paths.
```

Write .migration/flows/{flow-id}.md:

```
# Flow: {name}
Confidence: {score}
Trigger: {type} — {entry point} [{file}:{line}]

## Call Chain [CONFIRMED via AST | confidence: {score}]
